{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"reasoning","text":"**Encoding updated sanitize_email code**\n\n{\"code\":\"    def sanitize_email(self, text: str) -> str:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Replace all email addresses with ``[REDACTED_EMAIL]``.\\n\\n        BUG_65: the regex ``[\\\\\\\\w.]+@[\\\\\\\\w.]+`` does not include ``+``\\n        in the local-part character class, so plus-addressed emails\\n        like ``user+tag@domain.com`` are **not** redacted.\\n        Should be ``[\\\\\\\\w.+]+@[\\\\\\\\w.]+``.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        email_re = re.compile(r\\\"[\\\\w.+]+@[\\\\w.]+\\\")\\n        result = email_re.sub(_REDACTED_EMAIL, text)\\n        count = len(email_re.findall(text))\\n        self._history.append(\\n            SanitizationResult(text=result, emails_redacted=count)\\n        )\\n        orgops.compliance.record_decision(\\\"pii.sanitized\\\")\\n        return result\",\"comments\":\"Use a plus-aware regex for email redaction and log the pii.sanitized compliance decision.\"}"}}
